  "seoTitle": "Indonesia Enacts Law On Asset Seizure",
  "metaDescription": "Indonesia has enacted a new asset seizure law targeting crimes including corruption, online gambling, and terrorism, while excluding illicit enrichment.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "The new Indonesian law allows authorities to seize assets linked to offenses including corruption, online gambling, fraud, and terrorism.",
    "Legislators excluded provisions concerning illicit enrichment, a decision that has drawn criticism from civil society groups like the ICW.",
    "Regional legal offices have begun reviewing the application of the legislation to specific ongoing criminal proceedings."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian House of Representatives has formally ratified legislation concerning the seizure of criminal assets. According to government officials, the law grants authorities expanded powers to confiscate assets derived from various illicit activities, such as online gambling, fraud related to Umrah travel services, and acts of terrorism. The framework is intended to facilitate the recovery of losses sustained by victims of these crimes. However, the legislative process has prompted debate following the decision to omit regulations regarding illicit enrichment. The Indonesian Corruption Watch (ICW) has expressed criticism toward the legislature for this exclusion, arguing that it weakens the law's overall impact. Meanwhile, regional authorities, such as the High Prosecutor's Office in West Nusa Tenggara, are already evaluating how the new legal provisions can be integrated into existing criminal cases to address asset recovery efforts.",
